target/
*.log
evaluation*.json
run*.json

# Ambient tooling artifacts. Background daemons, editors and indexers on a developer's
# machine write into whatever directory they are pointed at — including a benchmark
# worktree. Anything matched here is environment noise, not agent output, and must never
# be counted as a scope violation by the evaluator.
.DS_Store
.memdb/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.pid
*.swp
# Note the trailing `/*` rather than `/`: git will not re-include anything inside a directory
# it has already excluded, so `.claude/` plus `!.claude/hooks/` silently ignores the hook and
# leaves the repo looking as though it has a reviewer it never committed.
.claude/*
# ...except the committed review hook. These two are TRACKED, so the evaluator's scope guard
# sees them only when an agent actually edits them — which is a real violation and should
# fail AC6. Everything else under .claude/ (settings.local.json, caches, whatever a daemon
# drops there) stays ignored, so the ambient-noise reason for the rule above is intact.
#
# This matters because the guard's second source is `git ls-files --others
# --exclude-standard`, which respects this file: an untracked .claude/ artifact would
# otherwise read as an unrelated changed file and fail a run for something the agent
# never did.
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
.copilot/
